    "content": {
      "value": "> **Who this is for:** Business Analysts\n> **Stages covered:** Stage 1 (Story Intake) and Stage 2 (AC Authoring)\n> **Prerequisite:** Read the [AI-Assisted QA — Overview & Methodology](../277544962) first.\n\n---\n\nWhat This Guide Covers\n----------------------\n\nThis guide explains how to structure a Jira story so that Claude can generate high-quality, Zephyr-ready acceptance criteria (AC) from it — and how to prompt Claude correctly to get output that needs minimal rework.\n\nThe output of Stage 2 is a set of approved Given/When/Then acceptance criteria attached to the Jira story, with the story status set to **AC Approved**. Nothing moves to Zephyr until that status is set.\n\n---\n\nStage 1 — Preparing the Jira Story\n----------------------------------\n\nBefore you prompt Claude, the story needs to be well-formed. A vague story produces vague AC. Claude is only as good as the context it is given.\n\n### The Story Template\n\nEvery Jira story on this programme must follow this structure in the **Description** field:\n\n`**User Role**\n[Who is performing this action — e.g. Guest Shopper, Registered Customer, Merchandiser]\n**Goal**\n[What they are trying to achieve — one sentence, from the user's perspective]\n**Context / Trigger**\n[What situation or action leads to this flow — e.g. \"Customer has added items to cart and proceeds to checkout\"]\n**In Scope**\n[What this story explicitly covers — be specific. List the flows, states, or interactions this story is responsible for.]\n**Out of Scope**\n[What this story does NOT cover — prevents AC from bleeding into adjacent stories]\n**Regions**\n[Which storefronts this story applies to — AU / UK / US DOM / US INTL / EU DOM / EU INTL / ME — or ALL]\n**Edge Cases to Consider**\n[Anything you already know about — empty states, validation errors, unavailable services, regional variants]\n**Jira Story Key**\n[The story key — e.g. ZIM-042 — used in test case naming]`\n\n### What Good Looks Like — Example\n\n`**User Role**\nGuest Shopper\n**Goal**\nComplete a domestic checkout as a guest without creating an account\n**Context / Trigger**\nCustomer has one or more items in their bag and clicks \"Checkout\" on the bag page.\nStorefront: AU (SFCC domestic checkout, Adyen payment, Avalara tax for NZ addresses only)\n**In Scope**\n- Full checkout journey: contact details → shipping address → shipping method → payment → order confirmation\n- Adyen card payment only (Apple Pay / Google Pay out of scope for this story — see ZIM-044)\n- Error handling: invalid card, declined card, address validation failure\n- Post-order: confirmation page renders with order number; confirmation email triggers\n**Out of Scope**\n- Registered customer checkout (see ZIM-043)\n- Express checkout / Apple Pay / Google Pay (see ZIM-044)\n- International checkout via Global-e (see ZIM-051)\n- Post-checkout account creation prompt (see ZIM-048)\n**Regions**\nAU only\n**Edge Cases to Consider**\n- Card declined by Adyen\n- Card number fails Luhn validation before submission\n- Shipping address outside AU (should not be reachable on AU storefront — confirm behaviour)\n- Didomi consent not given — confirm GTM purchase event does not fire\n**Jira Story Key**\nZIM-042`\n\n---\n\nStage 2 — Prompting Claude to Write AC\n--------------------------------------\n\n### The Prompt Template\n\nOnce your story is ready, open Claude (claude.ai) and use this prompt. Copy the entire block and fill in the bracketed sections.\n\n`You are writing acceptance criteria for a Jira story on the Zimmermann SFCC replatform —\na Magento 2 to Salesforce Commerce Cloud migration using PWA Kit on Managed Runtime,\nwith Adyen (domestic payments), Global-e (international checkout), Contentful (CMS),\nand MuleSoft (integration layer).\nHere is the story:\n---\n[PASTE YOUR FULL STORY DESCRIPTION HERE]\n---\nPlease write acceptance criteria using the Given/When/Then format. For each criterion:\n- Write one scenario per test case (not compound scenarios)\n- Use plain English — no technical jargon unless it is the correct term (e.g. \"Adyen\", \"Didomi\")\n- Cover: the happy path, all error paths in the In Scope section, and the edge cases listed\n- For each scenario, specify the region it applies to in brackets at the end — e.g. [AU] [ALL] [EU DOM + EU INTL]\n- Do not invent scope — if something is listed as Out of Scope, do not write AC for it\n- Number each acceptance criterion sequentially: AC-01, AC-02, etc.\nFormat each criterion as:\n**AC-[N]: [Short descriptive title]** [REGION]\n**Given** [precondition]\n**When** [action]\n**Then** [expected outcome]\n**And** [additional expected outcomes if needed]`\n\n### What Claude Will Produce\n\nClaude will return a numbered list of AC in the Given/When/Then format, one per scenario, tagged by region. A well-formed story typically produces between 6 and 15 AC items — fewer usually means edge cases were missed, more usually means the story scope is too wide.\n\n### Example Output (partial)\n\n`**AC-01: Guest completes checkout with a valid card** [AU]\n**Given** a guest shopper has one or more items in their bag\n**When** they complete all checkout steps and submit a valid Adyen card\n**Then** an order is created and the confirmation page displays the order number\n**And** an order confirmation email is triggered\n**AC-04: Card declined at payment step** [AU]\n**Given** a guest shopper has reached the payment step of checkout\n**When** they submit a card that Adyen declines\n**Then** an inline error message is displayed at the payment step\n**And** the customer remains on the payment step with their details retained\n**And** the order is not created\n**AC-07: GTM purchase event suppressed when consent not given** [AU]\n**Given** a guest shopper has completed checkout\n**And** they have not accepted analytics cookies via Didomi\n**When** the order confirmation page loads\n**Then** the GTM purchase event does not fire`\n\n---\n\nReviewing and Approving AC\n--------------------------\n\nThis is the most important step. Claude's output is a first draft. You must read every criterion before approving.\n\n### Review Checklist\n\nWork through each AC item and ask:\n\n* **Is the precondition (Given) accurate?** Does it match the actual state the user would be in?\n* **Is the action (When) specific enough?** \"Submits the form\" is better than \"clicks a button\" — but \"clicks the Place Order button\" is better still when the element is specific.\n* **Is the outcome (Then) testable?** \"The order is created\" is testable. \"The experience is good\" is not.\n* **Is the region tag correct?** An AU-only story should not have AC tagged [ALL].\n* **Are edge cases covered?** Check the story's Edge Cases section against the AC list.\n* **Is anything missing?** Common gaps: empty state when a list returns no results, service degradation (e.g. Didomi unavailable), accessibility (keyboard navigation, screen reader text).\n* **Is anything out of scope included?** Remove or redirect to the correct story.\n\n### Iterating with Claude\n\nIf the output needs changes, give Claude specific corrections rather than asking it to \"redo\" the whole thing:\n\n* \"AC-03 is missing the case where the address validation API is unavailable — add a degradation criterion.\"\n* \"AC-07 applies to EU DOM and EU INTL as well as AU. Update the region tag.\"\n* \"Combine AC-08 and AC-09 — they are the same scenario.\"\n\nClaude maintains context within the conversation, so you can iterate without re-pasting the full story.\n\n### Setting the Jira Status\n\nOnce you are satisfied with the AC:\n\n1. Copy the approved AC into the **Acceptance Criteria** field on the Jira story (or the Description if your project uses that field)\n2. Set the story status to **AC Approved**\n3. Comment on the Jira story: `AC approved [your name] [date]`\n\nThe story is now ready for Stage 3 — Zephyr test case creation.\n\n---\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\n------------------------\n\n| Mistake | Why It Matters | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Vague \"When\" step — \"user proceeds with checkout\" | Cannot be automated — the test runner needs to know what to click | Name the specific action: \"clicks the Proceed to Payment button\" |\n| Compound Then — \"order is created and email sends and page renders\" | One failure masks the others in test results | Split into separate And clauses or separate AC items |\n| Missing region tag | Tester doesn't know whether to run on all storefronts or one | Always tag, even if the answer is [ALL] |\n| AC covers Out of Scope items | Creates ambiguity about what the story is responsible for | Delete and note the correct story key |\n| Approving without reading | Claude drafts; the BA is accountable for the approved AC | Read every criterion — this is the human gate |\n\n---\n\nQuick Reference — AC Status Flow\n--------------------------------\n\n`Story drafted by BA\n│\n▼\nClaude generates AC draft\n│\n▼\nBA reviews and edits ──► iterate with Claude if needed\n│\n▼\nBA approves — sets Jira status to AC Approved ◀ HUMAN GATE 1\n│\n▼\nStory ready for Stage 3 — Zephyr test case creation`\n\n---\n\n*Last updated: June 2026 | Zimmermann Digital Modernisation — Accenture Song*",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "270d",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

