      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 4,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "> **Owner:** Integration Lead **Updated:** June 2026 **Purpose:** Single source of truth for all AI agents operating on the Zimmermann SFCC replatform programme — autonomous CI agents, interactive Claude Code CLI skills, and hybrid agents that combine both. Check this page before building any new agent capability to avoid duplication and ensure governance alignment.\n\n---\n\nWhat Counts as an Agent\n-----------------------\n\nFor the purposes of this registry, an **agent** is any AI-assisted capability that takes an action on behalf of a team member — whether that is raising a Jira ticket, creating a branch, generating a file, or guiding a developer through a fix. This includes:\n\n* **CI-automated agents** — triggered by GitHub Actions events, call AWS Bedrock, act without a human present\n* **Interactive agents** — Claude Code CLI skills invoked by a developer with a slash command\n* **Hybrid agents** — CI handles triage and admin autonomously; a Claude Code skill handles investigation and fix interactively\n\nCapabilities that only *read* and *summarise* (e.g. the Shared Brain RAG pipeline surfacing context into a conversation) are included for visibility but are lower governance priority than agents that *write* to systems.\n\n---\n\nGovernance Principles\n---------------------\n\nAll agents on this programme operate under the following non-negotiable constraints:\n\n* **Bedrock, not the Anthropic API** — all LLM calls from CI or automated contexts use AWS Bedrock. Claude Haiku for classification and routing decisions; Claude Sonnet for investigation, root cause analysis, and code generation.\n* **Tier 1 hard stop** — no agent writes to, modifies, or raises a PR touching Tier 1 files (design tokens, shared hooks, runtime config, CI workflows). Tier classification is always a deterministic CODEOWNERS check — never delegated to the LLM.\n* **No auto-merge** — agents can raise PRs but cannot merge them. Branch protection on `develop` and all `release/**` branches is enforced by GitHub and cannot be bypassed by any agent.\n* **Human gate on all code changes** — every PR raised by an agent requires a human developer to review and approve before merge.\n* **MCP for interactive Jira/Confluence writes; REST API for CI-automated writes** — the Atlassian MCP requires a persistent Claude Desktop session and cannot be called from a GitHub Actions runner. Interactive agents (Claude Code CLI skills) use the Atlassian MCP for Jira and Confluence writes. CI-automated agents use the Jira REST API v3 with a scoped service account token. All writes — via either path — carry the `agent-raised` label for auditability.\n* **Credentials in CI secrets only** — Bedrock credentials (AWS access key, secret, region), GitHub tokens, and Jira API tokens are stored as GitHub Actions secrets. Never committed to source control. Never passed through the LLM context.\n\n---\n\nAgent Registry\n--------------\n\n| Agent | Type | Trigger | Bedrock Model | Tier Access | Status | TSD |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AI-Assisted Defect Triage Agent | Hybrid | CI: BrowserStack failure event / Interactive: `/defect-triage` slash command | Haiku (classification) + Sonnet (investigation & fix) | Tier 2–4 (auto-fix); Tier 1–2 (investigation only, no code write) | 🟡 In Development | TSD: AI-Assisted Defect Triage Agent |\n| Shared Brain RAG Pipeline | Read-only | Nightly scheduled job + on-demand via Claude.ai | Sonnet (conflict analysis) | Read only — no writes to any system | 🟡 In Development | TSD pending |\n| Upstream Sync Watcher | CI-automated | GitHub: new release tag on Salesforce PWA Kit upstream repo | Haiku (diff summary) | Read only — raises a Jira notification ticket | 🟡 In Development | TSD pending |\n| `/generate-changelog` Skill | Interactive | Claude Code CLI slash command | Sonnet | Read only — outputs markdown for human to publish | 🟢 Live | TSD pending |\n| `/qa-generate` Skill | Interactive | Claude Code CLI slash command | Sonnet | Read only — outputs Gherkin for Lead QA to review | 🟢 Live | TSD pending |\n| `/session-start` Skill | Interactive | Claude Code CLI slash command | Sonnet | Read only — project health check and context load | 🟢 Live | TSD pending |\n| `/scope-check` Skill | Interactive | Claude Code CLI slash command | Sonnet | Read only — blast radius analysis, no writes | 🟢 Live | TSD pending |\n| `/feature-spec` Skill | Interactive | Claude Code CLI slash command | Sonnet | Read only — outputs spec for human review | 🟢 Live | TSD pending |\n\n---\n\nRegistry Schema\n---------------\n\nEach agent entry in the table above uses the following fields. When adding a new agent, all fields are mandatory.\n\n| Field | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Agent name** | Human-readable name. Link to the TSD once it exists. |\n| **Type** | `CI-automated` / `Interactive` (Claude Code CLI skill) / `Hybrid` / `Read-only` |\n| **Trigger** | What starts the agent — CI event, slash command, scheduled job, webhook |\n| **Bedrock model** | Which model(s) are called and for what purpose. `None` for skills that don't call Bedrock directly. |\n| **Tier access** | Which file tiers the agent can read or write. Be specific — read vs write access are different. |\n| **Status** | 🟢 Live / 🟡 In Development / 🔴 Planned / ⚫ Deprecated |\n| **TSD** | Link to the Technical Solution Design page. Required before status moves to Live. |\n\n---\n\nAdding a New Agent\n------------------\n\nBefore building any new agent capability:\n\n1. Add a row to the registry table above with status 🔴 Planned\n2. Create a TSD as a child of this page using the existing TSD as a template\n3. Get the TSD reviewed by the Integration Lead before build begins\n4. Update status to 🟡 In Development when build starts\n5. Update status to 🟢 Live when deployed to production\n\nA PR that introduces a new agent file (`.github/workflows/`, `.claude/skills/`, or a Bedrock invocation script) without a corresponding registry update will be flagged by CodeRabbit and must not be merged until the registry is current.\n\n---\n\n*Last updated: June 2026 | Zimmermann Digital Modernisation — Accenture Song*",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f916",
    "page_width": "max"
  }
}"}

